FLASHIA32.EFI:
51da3735757de1738ec239209498df12e4a65385ef16d772b81246a6e090d263

LIMITS
The firmware program runs before ExitBootServices, not inside the running
Zero kernel. The kernel has no runtime USB mass-storage driver yet.
The writer requires UEFI; BIOS remains supported for booting the system.
Native4Kn devices, unidentified/nonremovable USB devices and mounted/busy
native targets are rejected. Host programs are x86-64. Windows testing uses
Wine; QEMU/OVMF checks do not certify physical hardware or VirtualBox.
SHA256 supplies integrity, not publisher authentication. A write interrupted
by failure is not rolled back, and unused drive space is not securely wiped.

SOURCE AND DISTRIBUTION
Source composition, compilation, text encoding and archive packaging use
our Zero programs. Source archives exclude user data and screenshots.
A separate package receipt records extraction comparisons and a complete
rebuild from the frozen source archive. That receipt stays outside the
source archive to avoid a self-referential package checksum.
